<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36133" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phŏlŏē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φολόη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A forestclad mountain in Arcadia</i>, <i>on the borders of Elis</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 6,
				10, § 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2,
				273</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 10,
			228</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mountain in Thessaly</i>, <i>the
				abode of the Centaurs</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			198</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Achill. 1,
			138</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phŏlŏē-tĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Mount Pholoe</i>, <i>in Thessaly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">monstra,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the Centaurs</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 5, 230</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
